' =============================================================================
' Workflow Orchestration Engine — Sequence Diagrams
' =============================================================================
' Contains 10 diagrams covering the core execution flows.
'
' SYNC vs ASYNC convention used throughout:
'   -> (solid arrow)       = synchronous call (same call stack, blocking)
'   ->> (solid arrow)      = synchronous return
'   -[#BB0000]>            = ASYNC handoff (queue enqueue, fire-and-forget)
'   -[#BB0000]>>           = ASYNC dequeue / callback arrival
'   ...                    = time gap (process boundary, user wait)
'
' Color assignments:
'   Engine / Core services  = SAP_BLUE (#0070F2)
'   Handlers                = SAP_GREEN (#107E3E)
'   External / Workers      = SAP_GOLD (#E9730C)
'   User / Actor            = SAP_PURPLE (#7C5CCC)
'   Queue                   = SAP_RED (#BB0000)
'   Database / Repos        = SAP_TEAL (#049F9A)
'   Publisher / Realtime    = SAP_NAVY (#002A5E)
'
' ASYNC BOUNDARY markers use red-colored dividers to clearly show
' where the call stack breaks and execution continues in a different
' process/context.
' =============================================================================


' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Diagram 1: Start Run → Entry Node Dispatch
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@startuml start_run_flow

